@startuml
title DASHI TOE — singular-basin / coarse-RG obstruction convergence

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Existing theorem owners" {
  component "SingularBasinReductionExact" as Reduction
  component "SingularBasinFiniteWitnessExact" as Finite
  component "BasinResolutionRobustnessExact" as Resolution
  component "SingularBasinResolutionWitnessExact" as ResolutionWitness
  component "SingularBasinValidatedNumericsArtifactExact" as Validated
  component "YanchukStableManifoldCrossingTargetExact" as Yanchuk
  component "RGObservableInvariance" as PositiveRG
}

package "Normalized DASHI/Unified facade" {
  component "SingularBasinCoarseRGTOEExact" as Facade
  component "SingularBasinCoarseRGTOEValidation" as Validation
}

package "TOE consumers" {
  component "EverythingTOESymmetryResolved369" as TOE
  component "Unifier" as Unifier
  component "Unified.Everything" as Unified
}

Reduction --> Facade : generic non-preservation
Finite --> Facade : exact finite collision
Resolution --> Facade : resolution robustness
ResolutionWitness --> Facade : exact obstruction witness
Validated --> Facade : checker-soundness boundary
Yanchuk --> Facade : selected physical proof wall
PositiveRG ..> Facade : preservation surface; obstruction dual

Facade --> TOE
Facade --> Unifier
TOE --> Validation
Unifier --> Validation
Validation --> Unified

note bottom of Facade
Preconditions:
- canonical theorem owners already exist
- source attribution stays unchanged
- ESD surfaces are read-only

Invariants:
- finite witness is not the Yanchuk ODE
- numerical receipts do not create analytic theorems
- coarse projection does not imply basin-label preservation
- same reduced state plus different basin membership blocks exact factorisation

Postconditions:
- TOE and Unifier expose the same exact obstruction owners
- resolution non-robustness is reachable from the TOE graph
- interval ODE checker, checkerSound, interval manifold tube,
  and two-sided basin separation remain explicit open obligations
end note

@enduml
